Governance: Targeting & Send Settings
SEG-001 · Hard Fail · Base segment must be exactly one of:
CORE__ALL_ACTIVE_USERS | CORE__ALL_KNOWN_USERS | CORE__MARKETABLE_USERS
CORE__CUSTOMERS | CORE__PROSPECTS | CORE__VALID_USERS
SEG-002 · Hard Fail · Segment name must not contain:TEST | QA | INTERNAL | SEED
SEG-004 · Hard Fail · Must satisfy one of:
· Option A: CORE__VALID_USERS as base or AND filter
· Option B: "External User ID is not blank" + "Email Available is true"
FREQ-001 · Warn · Send date overlap across active campaigns:
· HIGH: same segment + same channel
· LOW: one matches (segment or channel)
· Cross-campaign data not visible = To Be Checked
UI-REF · Scheduling UI behaviour for campaign:
·Scheduled: Intelligent Timing is a scheduling option. Quiet Hours only appear when Intelligent Timing selected.
·Action-Based: No Intelligent Timing. Quiet Hours always visible as standalone checkbox.
·API-Triggered: No Intelligent Timing. Quiet Hours may not be visible.
QUIET-001 · Warn · Quiet hours must be enabled for Push or SMS:
·Flag if unchecked in following instances:Scheduled + Intelligent Timing active or Action-Based
·When Push/SMS detected in Canvas: verify Quiet hours enabled at Send Settings and at each Push/SMS step
TIME-001 · To Be Checked · Intelligent Timing:
· Enabled → confirm strategic intent with campaign owner
· Action-Based or API-Triggered → not applicable, do not flag
RE-001 · To Be Checked · Re-entry:
· Send once → N/A, skip all re-entry rules including CC-LRC-002, CC-001, CC-002, CC-003
· Otherwise → read checkbox state directly:
  Campaign: Schedule Delivery tab → Delivery Controls
  Canvas: Target Audience tab
· CHECKED → capture exact time window shown
· UNCHECKED → report as disabled
LEGEND:
· Hard Fail = must fix before launch
· Warn = review with campaign owner
· To Be Checked = confirm before launch. Never use "Governance Gap"
